Bound readback copies to the current frame allocation requirement.

Upstream pools encoder buffers. If host growth succeeds before device
growth fails, the retained host buffer can be larger than its GPU twin.
A retry at a smaller budget must copy the current requirement rather
than the host buffer capacity.

--- a/pyrowave_c.cpp
+++ b/pyrowave_c.cpp
@@ -1124,8 +1124,9 @@
 	// Performance issue since these memory types are mapped coherent on the GPU.
 	// A staging copy is just better. Could avoid it on iGPU, but iGPU isn't really supposed to be
 	// used as the encoder when streaming.
-	cmd->copy_buffer(*context.queued_meta, *context.queued_meta_gpu);
-	cmd->copy_buffer(*context.queued_bitstream, *context.queued_bitstream_gpu);
+	cmd->copy_buffer(*context.queued_meta, 0, *context.queued_meta_gpu, 0,
+	                 encoder->encoder.get_meta_required_size());
+	cmd->copy_buffer(*context.queued_bitstream, 0, *context.queued_bitstream_gpu, 0, bufinfo.size);
 
 	cmd->barrier(VK_PIPELINE_STAGE_2_COPY_BIT, VK_ACCESS_TRANSFER_WRITE_BIT,
 				 VK_PIPELINE_STAGE_HOST_BIT, VK_ACCESS_HOST_READ_BIT);
